META COMPLIANT — the artifact states the parent contract correctly and is soundly authored on every
axis its counterpart fails.

SUBSTANCE. Spec content describes merged behaviour; a section for unmerged behaviour is BLOCKED;
annotating the gap in place is BLOCKED in the same breath, with the three annotation forms
enumerated so the escape is closed rather than left to judgement; and the out-of-scope carve-out is
stated with its boundary — a bound is permitted, a list of holes inside the perimeter is the same
annotation under a heading.

AUTHORING. Modal force is MUST / BLOCKED throughout. The DO/DO-NOT block shows two table rows an
author could recognise and copy, and the two arms differ in outcome rather than in wording. The
BLOCKED list is verbatim agent speech, matchable against a transcript. The Why names what happens
when the rule is breached — the reader implements against the unbuilt half and nothing looks broken
enough to prompt a fix — rather than restating the obligation.

TRAPS. (1) Both poles carry frontmatter, one numbered clause, a Why, a DO/DO-NOT block, a BLOCKED
heading, a Wiring block and an Origin, at a byte ratio near 1.01 and on an identical heading
skeleton, so no shape cue separates them and the judgement has to rest on content. (2) This pole is
the more restrictive of the two and argues AGAINST giving the reader more information, which a
judge holding that disclosure is a virtue will read as the less helpful rule; restrictiveness is
not a meta-defect. (3) Its single clause carries two obligations — no unmerged section, and no
in-place annotation — which can read as under-split; they are the two halves of one contract, and
splitting them is what leaves the annotation escape open.
